1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK, before the first git write in your clone.** Read whole: RD-894 by Jira GET (`/rest/api/3/issue/RD-894?fields=summary,status,description,comment`; any JQL starts `project = RD AND ( ... )` WITH the parentheses; use NexusAI's read module: read `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/b774/b774lib.py` whole, load it with `python3 -I` through `importlib`, call only `get`, `search` and `adf_texts`; write verbs NOT yours); RD-891 (the fix this pins) by the same read; a search `project = RD AND ( text ~ "probeWritable" OR text ~ "rd891-probe-name-race" OR text ~ "write-test" )` (list the keys; if a ticket OTHER than RD-894 now covers one of the three cells, STOP naming it); `/usr/bin/grep -n -i -E 'RD-894|RD-891|C-190|C-68\b|C-209|C-57\b|C-89\b|C-224' '/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md' | cut -c1-300` (control: `RD-zzz9` prints none) and read the hits on the counts rule, the landing rule and any RD-891/RD-894 note (by line range; the Read tool refuses the file whole); the gate record `Briefs/2026-10-27_B827_STATUS.md` (findings B827-1 to B827-4, the mutant table at lines 155-162, the notes), the builder record of the fix it gated (`Briefs/2026-10-27_B816_STATUS.md` if present), and the sibling test-only builder `Briefs/2026-10-27_B849_STATUS.md` (the counts precedent and the empty-string lesson: a cell row that is green at base is a CONTROL by name, not a failure; here every new cell is green at base by design); in your clone `git --no-optional-locks log --format='%h %s' -8 -- __tests__/rd891-probe-name-race.test.js backend/jsonStorage.js`; the open PRs and `b8*`, `b9*`, `records/*` branches (any touching your paths => STARTABLE NO). **A READY FOR QA, PARTIAL or STOPPED without a PRIOR WORK section naming what you read and found is returned unread.** PRIOR WORK must say what the change PRESERVES, each with its measurement: the 8 existing cells (same names, same statuses, same `Tests:`