8. **Locks and load, by path.** The jest lock is the project's only jest mutex: `NEXUSAI_LOCK_BASE=/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/'!CODING'/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/locks-laptop-1017 bash /Volumes/Laptop-DEV/'!CODING'/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh jest b855-build-<step> <command>` (hash checked; usage from the tool's header `sed -n 1,40p`, never by invoking it to read it); FIFO; tag every ticket `b855-build-<step>`; `ls -la` of `queue-jest/` before and after each; never touch another seat's ticket, holder or tree; never `--replace` or `--after` a ticket that is not yours. Every jest run, mutant run and verify is a ticket. Hold limits: verify or `--update-counts` at most 35 minutes, any other ticket at most 20. **The partner seat (B856) and a gate may hold the lock: WAIT, never refuse.** STOP only if the holder pid is gone while the directory still names it (report, never remove) or the holder's etime passes 150 minutes. If load1 stays at or above 7, wait (poll 30 s) and do light work meanwhile. Heartbeat per STATUS-NOW.
9. **Corrections beat this brief.** Where a line, count or name here differs from your clone's main, use what you read and list the difference under Corrections.
10. **Landing is not yours and follows the project's rule** (`CLARIFICATIONS.md` C-190 items 2 and 3, lines 2067-2068 at the drafter's read: "Merge path: open a PR from the gated branch, wait for CodeQL (a background wait that EXITS), then land the SAME commit. Never squash, never rebase ([[C-68]])"; "NEVER dismiss a code-scanning alert, from any side, and never touch the ruleset"). The landing is a head-pinned MERGE commit of the gated head. The counts file's own `_why` says it IS the CI gate's expectation; your branch changes it only by the project's regeneration rule, once.

