Write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-28_B855_STATUS.md` at Step 0 and update it after every Step and jest hold. **Its FIRST line is the placeholder** `B855 STATUS (placeholder, Step 0 running)`, replaced by the real title when Step 0 completes. It holds the Step-0 block (sha256s of source and copy, slot count with control, REFUSE counts with controls, pane name, `gh auth status` in words, `core.sshCommand` path, lock-tool hash, the `brief_seat: model=...` line, target and hard stop absolute), then one line per Step 1-8 (not started / running / done / STOPPED with evidence path). **The LAST LINE of the file is, while you work, `WORKING: <step and what is running, with a figure that moves>`;** write no `READY FOR QA`, `PARTIAL:`, `STOPPED:` or `BLOCKED:` line anywhere (not even as a quotation at the start of a line) until you mean it: the coordinator's watcher reads only the last line. Heartbeat every waiter and long loop into `session-tools/b855/logs/heartbeat.txt` at least every 30 s with a MOVING figure (a load1 reading, `unit i of N`, elapsed seconds, a log size); three beats unmoved = stuck: say so. Wait on a recorded pid (`kill -0`) or a done-marker file, never `pgrep -f` from a shell whose argv holds the pattern. **RESUME at about 80 percent of context:** `WORKING: RESUME NEEDED at Step <n>` and a RESUME section (done, next command, paths, pids, commits so far).
