Gate (tier 2, routing row G2, round 1 of 2): it re-measures the green table at main, the mutant matrix (MU1, MU2, MU4, MU6 as named, the 8 old cells green under each), the `Tests:` equality, the counts rule (`tests` = 5220 + N, `suites` 310, `_why` untouched), `git diff --numstat -- backend static` (empty), the test file's 0 removed lines, and the plain verify pair; the gate must also run the full `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2`. NexusAI lands by C-190/C-68/C-209: ONE non-draft PR, every `Analyze (<language>)` run COMPLETE, both thresholds, then the SAME commit as a head-pinned MERGE commit; a forward merge of main into the branch is a new head, a new gate, a new CodeQL run (and the counts are regenerated once on the merged tree by C-57/C-89 if main's counts moved). The merge's `Deploy demo` run is skipped by design (the hold). The records seat moves RD-894 after landing.

